==> omaddons sync -h <==
Make every client match addons.toml

Usage: omaddons sync [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  The desired-state file, or - for stdin; default: addons.toml in config

Options:
      --strict   Exit 6 when only some of the addons sync
      --no-deps  Install only the listed addons, not the ones their TOCs require
      --locked   Install the versions the file records, from the blob cache when cached
      --prune    Also remove managed addons the file does not list

Examples:
  omaddons sync                       every client made to match addons.toml
  omaddons sync addons.toml --locked  the exact versions the file records
  omaddons sync - --prune --dry-run   a list piped in, previewed with what it would remove

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons sync --help <==
Make every client match addons.toml

Install what is missing, set pins and channels; never move an installed addon to a newer release
(that is update's job).

Usage: omaddons sync [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]
          The desired-state file, or - for stdin; default: addons.toml in config

Options:
      --strict
          Exit 6 when only some of the addons sync

      --no-deps
          Install only the listed addons, not the ones their TOCs require

      --locked
          Install the versions the file records, from the blob cache when cached

      --prune
          Also remove managed addons the file does not list
          
          Never one a listed addon requires or a lock names. Refused while a target section names no
          known client.

Examples:
  omaddons sync --dry-run                         what the file would change
  omaddons sync                                   install what is missing, set pins and channels
  omaddons sync dotfiles/addons.toml --locked     the exact versions the file records

The file (default: addons.toml in omaddons' config directory):

  schema_version = "1.0"

  [family.mainline]               # every live mainline client
  addons = ["WeakAuras", "DBM", "gh:BigWigsMods/BigWigs"]

  [[family.mainline.addon]]       # options: ref, channel, version, pinned
  name = "Plater"
  version = "Plater-v661"
  pinned = true

  [target."ptr"]                  # one client by id (the only way to reach a test client)
  addons = ["DBM"]

sync installs what is missing and sets pins and channels; it never updates an installed
addon (omaddons update does). A second run changes nothing. With --locked it installs
the version each entry records (from the download cache when it is still there), so
`omaddons export` on one machine and `sync --locked` on another reproduce the set.
With --prune it also removes managed addons the file does not list, never one a listed
addon requires or a lock names, and never on a client the file has no section for; a
section for no known client refuses it.

See also: export, update

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias:
                          --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Run only what the preview that returned this token showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
